<ul class="sources">
<li><a href="https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.212" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">29 CFR 1910.212, General requirements for all machines</a>, OSHA. Guarding for ingoing nip points and rotating parts.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.osha.gov/laws-regs/regulations/standardnumber/1910/1910.219" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">29 CFR 1910.219, Mechanical power-transmission apparatus</a>, OSHA. Guarding of shafts, pulleys, chains, and sprockets.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.energy.gov/sites/prod/files/2014/04/f15/motor_tip_sheet11.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Adjustable Speed Drive Part-Load Efficiency (Motor Systems Tip Sheet #11)</a>, U.S. Department of Energy. Conveyors as constant torque loads with power linear in speed.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.energy.gov/sites/default/files/2023-05/em-ecs-dfr.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Energy Conservation Standards for Electric Motors, Direct Final Rule</a>, U.S. Department of Energy (2023). Federal motor efficiency levels.</li>
</ul>
